SSH is one of the most common protocols in any enterprise environment, and one of the most frequently targeted by attackers.
SSH, stands for Secure Shell, is a cryptographic network protocol that establishes an encrypted connection between computers to allow for secure remote access over an unsecured network. 
It operates on TCP port 22 by default and is most notably used by system administrators and developers for remote command-line login and secure data execution.

Prerequisties
Ensure the following:
. Splunk Enterprise is installed and configured (Splunk Installation & Setup Guide).
. SSH log data sources are configured to forward logs to Splunk.